Z||000004||Robert||09-23-2000||02:38 PM||||I test road an electric car in the 70’s, could of passed for a phone booth.  It was a terrible ride, jerked you at the start and when it shifted.  <BR>Now for a totally awesome electric car, take a test ride in the EV1 at a Saturn dealership.  I had to make an appointment for the test ride, and listen to the sales/company pitch for about a half hour, but the drive was worth it.  If you can, schedule it in the evening to get the full effect of the digital dash.  If you are lucky and get a sales person who lets you “put the peddle to the metal”, your head is going to snap.  I acceleration is awesome.  It does have a limiter on it to keep it under 85MPH, but I’m telling you it doesn’t take long to get there.  I passed on the lease only option @ $399 per month, too much for a car that only has a 50 mile range. <BR>||||reg||1
